{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/design/dao.shibi.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# ShiBi\n     2\t\n     3\tStatus: stub. ShiBi is not specified and not implemented\n     4\t(`docs/bootstrap.md`, Capability Engine). This page records only what other\n     5\tdocuments may rely on and what ShiBi must supply. It designs nothing.\n     6\t\n     7\t## What it is\n     8\t\n     9\tShiBi is the capability system of datom.world: authentication and\n    10\tauthorization are its job and no other document's. It is to be built the\n    11\tway `dao.space` is built, as a tuple space that emerges from two\n    12\tinterpreters over ordinary streams, one that indexes and one that queries,\n    13\tneither knowing the other exists (`datom.world.md`, Streams). Its tokens are\n    14\tdescribed elsewhere as Macaroon-style: attenuatable, offline-verifiable,\n    15\trevocable caveats (`dao.space.security.md`, Capabilities Govern\n    16\tInterpreters).\n    17\t\n    18\t## How it plugs in\n    19\t\n    20\tShiBi integrates through the middleware seam of\n    21\t[`dao.stream.middleware.md`](./dao.stream.middleware.md) and the attachment\n    22\tpoints of [`dao.stream.remote.md`](./dao.stream.remote.md) section 7, which\n    23\tare fixed and which ShiBi must not change. The fit to two interpreters is\n    24\tthis, and it is the one path this version chooses:\n    25\t\n    26\t- **Its index interpreter** observes ShiBi's fact streams (grants,\n    27\t  caveats, revocations, emitted decisions) with its own cursors,\n    28\t  materializes them as `dao.space.index` materializes covered indexes, and\n    29\t  publishes the resulting immutable query value, a relation value or an\n    30\t  opened published index, as the decision onto the gate's capacity-1\n    31\t  decision medium (`dao.stream.middleware.md`, gate). The value published\n    32\t  is the tuple space's state at that moment.\n    33\t- **Its query interpreter is `verify`**, and `verify` is the required\n    34\t  adapter contract: a pure function of one immutable query value, the\n    35\t  context and the request, evaluating ShiBi's authorization rules as a\n    36\t  Datalog query with the request as bindings, the shape\n    37\t  `dao.space.query/q` already has (a query over immutable inputs, opening\n    38\t  nothing), and answering nil or a reason.\n    39\t- **A `present`**, a pure function of context and request that produces\n    40\t  the value carried in `:dao.stream.remote/credential`.\n    41\t- **A reason vocabulary** under its own namespace for\n    42\t  `:dao.stream.middleware/reason`.\n    43\t- **Where use is metered**, the decision facts the gate emits, which the\n    44\t  index observes like any other fact stream.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Limits of the adapter contract**, stated precisely. `verify` runs\n    47\tsynchronously inside one operation on one snapshot: its cost per operation\n    48\tis bounded by the composition, and a query over an opened published index\n    49\tresolves only what is already local, because `verify` opens, fetches and\n    50\twaits for nothing; a rule that would need a remote read is a rule the index\n    51\tmust have materialized. Its input is the latest published snapshot, so a\n    52\tgrant or revocation is effective only once the index has observed and\n    53\tpublished it: staleness is bounded by the index's cadence and the medium's\n    54\teviction, and a policy that must fail closed does so on the `none` marker\n    55\tand the `ended` marker. A decision is per call and is not itself a fact\n    56\tunless the gate emits it.\n    57\t\n    58\t**Non-goal in this version.** Request-specific decisions published through\n    59\tordinary streams, the query interpreter reading requests off a stream and\n    60\tappending one decision per request for the gate to await, are not\n    61\tspecified: a gate awaiting a per-request answer would wait, and no\n    62\toperation waits. If a later ShiBi needs that path it is an addition beside\n    63\t`verify`, not a change to it.\n    64\t\n    65\tThe contract's refusal outcome is `:dao.stream/refused` and is\n    66\tcapability-free (`dao.stream.md`, Result Convention). Lease attribution\n    67\trests on per-author media and does not depend on ShiBi\n    68\t(`dao.stream.remote.md`, section 6; `yin.repl.link-policy.md`).\n    69\t\n    70\t## What blocks it being load-bearing\n    71\t\n    72\t`dao.stream.discovery.md`, The ShiBi precondition: ShiBi is a capability\n    73\ttoken in one place and a fungible currency in another, and a currency needs\n    74\tdouble-spend resolution, which is global consensus. Until that decision is\n    75\tmade, no design may depend on ShiBi for anything beyond the seam above, and\n    76\tgating in this repository is an allow-list or a pre-shared value.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
