{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/dao.space.stigmergy.md | sed -n '235,251p'\"","aggregated_output":"   235\tquery rule, exactly as predicted.\n   236\t\n   237\t## The minimum viable stack\n   238\t\n   239\tFor a working multi-agent system on today's code, trusted agents only — no coordinator, no\n   240\tdeposit API, no new namespaces:\n   241\t\n   242\t1. **Historical implementation:** today's `dao.jing.file` content handle\n   243\t   used `dao.jing.remote/default-handlers` and\n   244\t   `dao.jing.remote/connect-content!`. `dao.jing.remote` is deprecated\n   245\t   whole; the planned successor is `dao.jing.content` over\n   246\t   `dao.stream.remote.md` (see its implementation plan). Both handles\n   247\t   expose the same plain-data content effects.\n   248\t2. **Writes**: each agent owns a local `dao.stream` memory-log and creates one\n   249\t   transactor value with that stream plus an explicit DaoJing intake pool\n   250\t   (`dao.space.transactor/create!`). It commits entity maps or datom vectors\n   251\t   through `transactor/append!`/`transact!`, using integer stream-local entity ids; the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
